<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">Why time has an arrow</p>
    <h2 id="t-arrow">The Past Was Special</h2>
    <p>Microscopic equations are often reversible while macroscopic records are not. Statistical mechanics
      explains the overwhelmingly likely direction of change given an extraordinarily low-entropy boundary
      condition in the past. It does not yet explain why that boundary condition obtained. Cosmology calls
      this the Past Hypothesis problem.</p>
    <p>TTI&rsquo;s <a href="/seams/#t-arrow">geometric arrow</a> and
      <a href="/temporal-antipodes/">Temporal Antipodes</a> offer metaphysical pictures of that boundary.
      They do not replace the probability measure, the microscopic dynamics or the low-entropy initial
      condition. A picture becomes physics only when it reproduces those ingredients and risks a contrary
      observation.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap reveal">
  <div class="grid two">
    <article class="frame card">
      <p class="kicker">TTI &middot; retained proposal</p>
      <h2 id="t-integration-phases">Phases as Levels of Integration</h2>
      <p>The transferred EGregoRA essay proposed a ladder from possibility, through partial coherence, to
        durable matter and reflective integration. TTI retains the useful question: can one define an order
        parameter \(I\) that measures coordinated causal participation rather than merely naming it?</p>
      <p>A credible \(I\) would have units or be explicitly dimensionless, remain invariant under harmless
        changes of description, specify the system boundary, and predict something not already built into its
        definition. Until then, &ldquo;phase&rdquo; is philosophical language, not a discovered phase of matter.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card">
      <p class="kicker">Historical material &middot; preserved, not promoted</p>
      <h2 id="t-symbolic-poles">101, 333, 666 and 999</h2>
      <p>The earlier page arranged these numbers as symbolic poles of initiation, formation, material
        completion and return. Their repeating digits, and the fact that \(666=T_{36}\), can support a
        cultural or numerological reading. They do not follow from Boltzmann entropy, quantum field theory or
        cosmological data.</p>
      <p>The arithmetic material belongs with the <a href="/spiral/">triangular-number spiral</a> and
        <a href="/skeletal-splice/">Skeletal Splice</a>, where exact identities can be checked before a
        cosmological meaning is considered. Symbolic resonance is retained here as history of the framework,
        not entered as physical evidence.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">A derivation gate</p>
    <h2 id="t-bridge">What a Real Entropy&ndash;Integration Bridge Would Need</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><strong>State space:</strong> define the microstates, macrostates and system boundary.</li>
      <li><strong>Dynamics:</strong> state how probabilities evolve and whether the evolution is reversible.</li>
      <li><strong>Order parameter:</strong> define integration independently of the effect it is meant to explain.</li>
      <li><strong>Bridge law:</strong> derive a relation such as \(I=F[\rho]\), rather than relying on verbal resemblance.</li>
      <li><strong>Null models:</strong> compare against ordinary equilibration, self-organisation and gravitational clumping.</li>
      <li><strong>Loss condition:</strong> name a measurement that could show the proposed bridge is absent.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="lede">Without those six items, the safe statement is that entropy and integration are two
      descriptions that may move together, move oppositely or be independent, depending on the system.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap reveal">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">Six categories, kept apart</p>
    <h2 id="t-scorecard">The Scorecard</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="grid three">
    <div class="frame card"><h3>Physical <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></h3><p>Thermodynamic inequalities, statistical ensembles, quantum density matrices and measured transport belong here.</p></div>
    <div class="frame card"><h3>Mathematical <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></h3><p>Logarithms, probability distributions and exact combinatorial identities are valid independently of TTI.</p></div>
    <div class="frame card"><h3>Informational <span class="hist">&#9670;</span></h3><p>Shannon uncertainty is rigorous; its physical cost depends on an embodied protocol.</p></div>
    <div class="frame card"><h3>Philosophical <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></h3><p>Integration as becoming offers an interpretation of organised wholes, not a measured state variable yet.</p></div>
    <div class="frame card"><h3>Spiritual <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></h3><p>Return, initiation and wholeness may guide meaning without being presented as thermodynamic findings.</p></div>
    <div class="frame card"><h3>Cultural <span class="hist">&#9670;</span></h3><p>The number-pole sequence records the framework&rsquo;s history and symbolic vocabulary.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

